---
/**
 * The animated page background, plus the scrim that keeps text on top of it
 * readable. Both are fixed to the viewport and neither is in the flow, so the
 * layout above is unaware of them.
 *
 * Two elements rather than one because they are two different contracts: the
 * canvas is progressive enhancement and may legitimately never paint, while
 * the scrim is what the contrast ratios in design.md §7 are measured against
 * and therefore has to exist whether or not WebGL does.
 *
 * `aria-hidden` on the wrapper: it is a background. Styles live in global.css
 * with the rest of the layout, and the shader in scripts/veil.ts.
 */
---

<div class="veil" aria-hidden="true">
  <canvas data-veil></canvas>
  <div class="veil-scrim"></div>
</div>

<script src="../scripts/veil.ts"></script>
